# Session Management Rules

## Start of Every Session
1. Read `DEVLOG.md` — check what was done last and what's left
2. Read `CURSOR_KICKOFF.md` — understand the full build plan
3. Confirm your understanding before writing code

## End of Every Session
Append a new entry to `DEVLOG.md` with this format:

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD - [Codex|Claude|Cursor] Short title

### What was built
- File changes with brief descriptions

### What's working
- ✅ items that compile and function

### What's left
- [ ] remaining tasks

### Gotchas
- Any bugs, surprises, or non-obvious patterns discovered

### Current state
Build status and any blockers
```

The entry header above is the canonical form from `AGENTS.md` ("Handoff
Discipline"); that section is the source of truth for the section list, so
follow it if the two ever drift.

## Commit Discipline
- One shippable commit per fix, and only when Brian asks for a commit
- Run build verification before every commit
- Tag rollback points as `checkpoint/*` (e.g. `checkpoint/appstore-prep-2026-07-11`) before any multi-commit run
